! ============================================================
! 01b  Geometry optimization
! ============================================================
! The same molecule, now allowed to relax.  The starting
! geometry is deliberately distorted (O-H stretched to 1.10 A,
! angle opened to 115 deg) so that you can watch it come back.
!
! WHAT TO LOOK AT:
!   * the optimizer table: max|g| must fall monotonically.
!     It is the GRADIENT, not the energy, that tells you the
!     structure has converged -- the energy is flat near a
!     minimum and stops changing long before the geometry does.
!   * the final structure: r(OH) ~ 0.99 A, angle ~ 100 deg.
!
! HF/STO-3G gets the bond length ~3 % too long and the angle
! ~4 deg too small (experiment: 0.958 A, 104.5 deg).  That is
! the expected quality of a minimal basis, not a program error;
! example 02a shows what fixes it.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%charge  0
%mult    1

%geo
 O   0.0000000   0.0000000   0.1500000
 H   0.0000000   0.9300000  -0.5500000
 H   0.0000000  -0.9300000  -0.5500000
